{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1444098-moon-paths-moon-glows-and-penumbral-hazards","id":1444098,"title":"Moon Paths, Moon Glows, and Penumbral Hazards","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-04-15T17:17:39-07:00","id":1444098,"title":"Moon Paths, Moon Glows, and Penumbral Hazards","content":"I've been completely neglecting something in my chronicles. There is a talen called a Moon Glow which protects umbral travelers from incidental umbral hazards (like hostile spirits attacking the Garou). I've never actually used this, but now want to make sure it is useful. However, in order to do so, I have to think of incidental umbral hazards that would normally happen. Because if I don't include them in the game, there's no benefit to using the talen.<br /> <br /> I don't normally have such hostile spirits unless the Garou intend to attack something in the Umbra. So while I might use Moon Glow to allow the PCs to avoid encounters until they reach their destination, it still seems like I am not having enough potential danger. So I wanted to research the description of the Penumbra and Umbral travel in more detail to see if I am neglecting anything.<br /> <br /> Because a Moon Glow is created by binding a Lune, I reasoned the reason the Moon Glow works is probably because other spirits think you are a Lune, and they are choosing to avoid interaction with Lunes. I remembered something like that in the rules. So I found it. That's found in the section concerning Moon Paths. We're told Moon Paths are defended by Lunes during the full moon, and that hostile spirits stay out of reach of them, just beyond sight (they gather because they can see the Moon Path and are hoping any Garou would foolishly step away from it, but can't directly attack the Moon Path because the Lunes are too powerful). Moon Paths become more dangerous in other phases of the moon, and are very dangerous during the new moon because there's no Lunes guarding one. So that's exactly what I am looking for.<br /> <br /> However, I just realized something. At no point does the book actually tell me what Moon Paths connect. I know a Moon Bridge connects two caerns. I know you can walk through the Penumbra like normal. I know Gates exist that can permanently connect a point in the Umbra to another point in the Umbra. I know spirit airts are tracks made by the travel of spirits, acting like deer trails in a forest that can be followed. And I know that quests to the Near Realms involve lots of esoteric travel finding the right spiritual correspondences that lead you deeper and deeper into the umbra.<br /> <br /> But I don't know what Moon Paths actually do. The book says they exist as shafts of moonlight in the mists of the Penumbra, and that entering their light allows you to travel on the moonbeam. But nothing else is said about where they lead.<br /> <br /> Are they simply a Storyteller device to provide a shortcut to some destination? Can you use them to travel to someplace other than the Penumbra? How does one know where the Moon Path would take you? Can you determine where you go, like pushing buttons on an elevator to select your floor, or is the destination pre-determined, or is it completely random?<br /> <br /> I searched online to learn more, but all references simply repeat the information in the corebook and Umbra.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-16T02:13:25-07:00","id":1444142,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1444098-moon-paths-moon-glows-and-penumbral-hazards#post1444098\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've been completely neglecting something in my chronicles. There is a talen called a Moon Glow which protects umbral travelers from incidental umbral hazards (like hostile spirits attacking the Garou). I've never actually used this, but now want to make sure it is useful. However, in order to do so, I have to think of incidental umbral hazards that would normally happen. Because if I don't include them in the game, there's no benefit to using the talen.</div> </div> </div> </div>True. Umbra books of 2nd and revised edition talked about travel hazards. W20 Umbra might, too.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1444098-moon-paths-moon-glows-and-penumbral-hazards#post1444098\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because a Moon Glow is created by binding a Lune, I reasoned the reason the Moon Glow works is probably because other spirits think you are a Lune, and they are choosing to avoid interaction with Lunes.I remembered something like that in the rules. So I found it. That's found in the section concerning Moon Paths. We're told Moon Paths are defended by Lunes during the full moon, and that hostile spirits stay out of reach of them, just beyond sight (they gather because they can see the Moon Path and are hoping any Garou would foolishly step away from it, but can't directly attack the Moon Path because the Lunes are too powerful). Moon Paths become more dangerous in other phases of the moon, and are very dangerous during the new moon because there's no Lunes guarding one. So that's exactly what I am looking for.</div> </div> </div> </div>In our LARP it works like this:<br /> If activated a Moon Glow Talen will emit moonlight. This has two effects. First, all observers in some (undefined) distance will see the light and naturally assume a lune spirit is on the move. This will make most predatory gaian sprits think twice before approaching/attacking the group. It won't have any effect on spirits that would naturally attack a lune, like powerful banes, or affect any guardians who guard a specific place and are approached by the group that carries the moon glow.<br /> The second effect is, that the light emitted is considered moon light, and therefore makes the moon path reflect it in the vicinity. Normally, a moon path is best visible at full moon, and nigh invisible at new moon. But it is there, and the light from the Moon Glow will make it visible again. Since Moon Paths are stable, usually hazard free, paths through the penumbra, near umbra and realms, this makes for a relatively safe travel, even when the moon phase wouldn't allow it, or in areas where the moon isn't permanently visible.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1444098-moon-paths-moon-glows-and-penumbral-hazards#post1444098\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">However, I just realized something. At no point does the book actually tell me what Moon Paths connect</div> </div> </div> </div>Everything and nothing, I guess. The paths criss-cross, as far as I understood it, the penumbra, near umbra and realms. Partially they reach into the sky (and eventually the Atherial realm) and are save for they usually never change drastically. If you walk through the penumbra but not on a moon path, you may accidentally use these spiritual correspondences and engage in the esoteric travelling stuff you mentioned. With moon paths you are safe and usually able to return using the same way. Without the moon path, you have to rely on Perception and enigmas a lot (and wits, I guess). Umbra 2nd had some inspiration on that.<br /> Since the near Umbra and realms are basically infinite, there network of moon paths is too. Knowing a specific route from A to B, like from a moon path that comes close to the caern's bawn in the penumbra and leads to the Legendary Realm means to know in which direction to go first and then when to take which intersection along the route. And this will remain a valid route for the forseeable future, unlike other routes through the umbra, that are subject to change more often.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1444098-moon-paths-moon-glows-and-penumbral-hazards#post1444098\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But I don't know what Moon Paths actually do. The book says they exist as shafts of moonlight in the mists of the Penumbra, and that entering their light allows you to travel on the moonbeam.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is this a W20 reference? Or from what book is it, for it seems closer to a moon bridge description.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1444098-moon-paths-moon-glows-and-penumbral-hazards#post1444098\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are they simply a Storyteller device to provide a shortcut to some destination?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Gift &quot;Bridge Walker&quot; and the Charm &quot;Open Moon Bridge&quot; are independent from Caerns/Pathstones and are in my opinion the &quot;shortcut&quot; version. Moonpaths are more like a means to simplify travel. Like an Elder tells the pack:<br /> &quot;Go to Place X and step sideways, you will see a moonpath, follow it to the south and don't leave it for three days of lupus form travel, then you will reach an intersection, the 14th since you started, here you will take the path to your left, not sharp left, but leftish and follow it to a Glen domain. Rest there then follow the moon path that leaves the Glen near a triple palm tree. Follow it for four days and you will reach the outskirts of the Legendary Realm near a village that belongs to the legend of Beowolf...&quot;<br /> If the garou follow the instruction, and the moon light or a moon glow keep the path well visible all the time, than you can skip over adversarial or natural umbral hazards, but might add random encounter with other travelling fera or dreamspeaker mages (as Albrecht &amp; Co had in Silver Crown).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1444098-moon-paths-moon-glows-and-penumbral-hazards#post1444098\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can you use them to travel to someplace other than the Penumbra?</div> </div> </div> </div>As far as I read 2ndand rev Edition, they go through all the Umbra.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1444098-moon-paths-moon-glows-and-penumbral-hazards#post1444098\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How does one know where the Moon Path would take you?</div> </div> </div> </div>Corax and Nuwisha might have Backgrounds to know such stuff. Others might only know though experience and legends. Moon Paths are, as I understood it, permanent. Landmarks along the paths might be subject to change, especially if people put an effort to it. A Glen Domain, that is laid waste to by banes might cease to exist. The moonpath leading there still will lead though there, but if your route description entails info like &quot;after the Glen, take the left path at then next T-Section&quot; become invalid&quot;.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1444098-moon-paths-moon-glows-and-penumbral-hazards#post1444098\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can you determine where you go, like pushing buttons on an elevator to select your floor, or is the destination pre-determined, or is it completely random?</div> </div> </div> </div>See above.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-16T02:28:09-07:00","id":1444144,"title":"","content":"Umbral winds or storms are listed as one hazard. I'm not sure how a Moon Glow would protect from that, but possibly they just happen less often to travellers with the Talen. In any case, I can't remember any specific rule, but would assume one Talen per day is sufficient, not one per scene. But the Talen has to be carried openly to function.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-16T10:48:15-07:00","id":1444223,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1444098-moon-paths-moon-glows-and-penumbral-hazards?p=1444142#post1444142\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is this a W20 reference? Or from what book is it, for it seems closer to a moon bridge description.</div> </div> </div> </div>All my descriptions are based on Revised since I have both the corebook and Umbra book of that edition. In my experience, Revised typically has the most detail and flavor text of the editions, but sometimes contradicts what was established in previous editions either on purpose or because the writer didn't actually understand or know the previous canon/rules.<br /> <br /> Page 233 of the Revised corebook states: <i>One of Luna's many gifts to her children are paths through the mists of the Umbra. A moon path appears in the Penumbra as a shaft of moonlight. A werewolf who touches the light can find herself traveling on a moonbeam with the mists of the spirit world swirling all around her.</i><br /> <br /> When I read things online, there are many references of Moon Bridges being a special type of Moon Path, but I don't know if that is actually per the rules or people's interpretations. But they are certainly similar - both relying on Luna to create a lunar route. It's just that Moon Paths seem to be &quot;natural&quot; while Moon Bridges are &quot;created&quot; by Garou between caerns using Pathstones.<br /> <br /> =<br /> <br /> Moon Paths being permanent and leading to fixed destinations is probably the easiest interpretation for the ST. They just need to decide where to plant any Moon Paths on his umbral map and determine where they go. I think the only hard decision is deciding how many Moon Paths should be out there and their destinations. I like to have maps in my head (or on paper) and know many important landmarks before I run my games, so I am probably making this harder on myself than most STs who likely only put a Moon Path in after they decide they need one.<br /> <br /> I'll begin using that definition as I work through this. But if people have other ideas, I'd still like to hear them.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-16T10:56:44-07:00","id":1444228,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1444098-moon-paths-moon-glows-and-penumbral-hazards?p=1444142#post1444142\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Corax and Nuwisha might have Backgrounds to know such stuff. Others might only know though experience and legends. Moon Paths are, as I understood it, permanent.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, if they are permanent, they just become part of the umbral landscape. And eventually they will get explored, and that information will get out there. It's just whether or not that specific Moon Path is known to your specific Garou PC, your PC's pack totem, or your sept. If it is, you know where it'll take you. If not, you have to explore it yourself. So any nearby Moon Paths within the sept protectorate's Penumbra should be fairly well known. But if you find one in the farther away, or &quot;deeper&quot; in the Umbra, the chances go down.<br /> <br /> As you said, in terms of characters who would have the most detailed knowledge of the Umbra and therefore a more accurate &quot;map&quot; of Moon Paths, the Corax and Nuwisha should know best. As well as Garou who specialize in Umbral travel like the Wagnerians and other camps.<br /> <br /> I figure that while Moon Paths are &quot;permanent&quot;, that really just means they are long standing features. But Luna likely both closes Moon Paths and creates new Moon Paths on occasion. She's supposed to be mercurial after all. Not to the point it gets confusing or collapse the entire system of Moon Paths, but it happens. So that could be an excuse for an ST to introduce a new plot for the PCs. &quot;Hey, a pack spotted a new Moon Path we had not seen before. We're looking for someone willing to explore it and report back to the sept. Why don't you PCs do it?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-16T11:04:29-07:00","id":1444231,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1444098-moon-paths-moon-glows-and-penumbral-hazards?p=1444142#post1444142\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In our LARP it works like this:<br /> If activated a Moon Glow Talen will emit moonlight. This has two effects. First, all observers in some (undefined) distance will see the light and naturally assume a lune spirit is on the move. This will make most predatory gaian sprits think twice before approaching/attacking the group. It won't have any effect on spirits that would naturally attack a lune, like powerful banes, or affect any guardians who guard a specific place and are approached by the group that carries the moon glow.<br /> The second effect is, that the light emitted is considered moon light, and therefore makes the moon path reflect it in the vicinity. Normally, a moon path is best visible at full moon, and nigh invisible at new moon. But it is there, and the light from the Moon Glow will make it visible again. Since Moon Paths are stable, usually hazard free, paths through the penumbra, near umbra and realms, this makes for a relatively safe travel, even when the moon phase wouldn't allow it, or in areas where the moon isn't permanently visible.</div> </div> </div> </div>That seems to be a solid basis from which to work from.<br /> <br /> I had not considered the idea that one threat would be Gaian spirits that are predatory, but it's a good idea. Are these mainly spirits of animal predators in your game? Or are they some other kind of predatory spirit? I normally don't have Gaian spirits attack Garou, but am open to the concept. How do you run that in your LARP?<br /> <br /> The Moon Path description during the full moon says &quot;dire spirits lurk near the edges&quot; which seems more like Banes to me. They're just afraid of the (many?) Lunes that normally guard the Moon Path. And these spirits might not be based in the Penumbra, but &quot;deeper&quot; in the Umbra as the Garou travel. So they might really only show up when Garou travel on Moon Paths during other phases of the Moon, particularly the new moon.<br /> <br /> I'll have to think of what kind of spirits that would be.<br /> <br /> I do think that in the Penumbra where certain Moon Paths originate, there could be local powerful Banes that are attracted there and will ambush Garou who approach if they think they have a good chance of winning, and these could be an example of a Bane that is not deterred by a Moon Glow.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-16T13:20:55-07:00","id":1444250,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1444098-moon-paths-moon-glows-and-penumbral-hazards?p=1444223#post1444223\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Page 233 of the Revised corebook states: <i>One of Luna's many gifts to her children are paths through the mists of the Umbra. A moon path appears in the Penumbra as a shaft of moonlight. A werewolf who touches the light can find herself traveling on a moonbeam with the mists of the spirit world swirling all around her.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>I see. The 2nd Edition core book isn't that detailed, but not contradicting this.<br /> <br /> Here is what &quot;Umbra: The Velvet Shadow&quot; state on page 23:<br /> <i>Once a Garou arrives in the Umbra, she must find her way through the Umbrascape. There are five major methods of transit through the Umbra.<br /> First, there are Moon Bridges. [...]<br /> Moon Paths are a second means of travel. At night, they appear in the Umbra when Luna shines. Some Garou use the terms Moon Bridges and Moon Paths interchangeably, but experienced Umbral travellers are careful to note the difference. Moon Paths crisscross the Umbra and connect most locales with one another. They are the most common means of travel within the Umbra for Garou.<br /> Moon Paths change depending on the phases of Luna. During the Full Moon, they are the safest means of travel and are guarded by Lunes all along their routes. During the Gibbous Moon, they may be partially incomplete; sometimes they require a special howl to open completely. At the Half Moon, the Moon Paths become hard to read. Some spirits take up residence on the Moon Paths during this time, negotiating with the travellers for passage. Wyldlings are notorious for this. During the Crescent Moon, the Moon Paths become virtually unreadable. A Garou has to roll Perception<br /> + Enigmas to be certain of the routes. Banes will ambush Garou travelling during the Crescent Moon. However, it is said that during the Crescent Moon the Moon Paths travel farther than they do at any other time. When Luna is the New Moon, the Moon Paths fade to near invisibility. Wyrrn minions roam freely across the Umbrascape, and only the wise can hide while finding the paths. The Moon Paths existing during the New Moon require Garou to solve mysteries within themselves. A Storyteller can require the Garou to make Charisma + Enigmas rolls at a difficulty equal to the Garou's Rage. It is said that the Moon Paths are shuffled along different routes during the New Moon.<br /> Garou travelling through the Umbra may encounter a number of hazards and strange difficulties. When Garou start taking a Moon Path, you can make them roll Intelligence + Rituals, with a difficulty determined by destination and familiarity with the route. For every success less than five, give them an encounter.</i><br /> <br /> This description, too, could mean that Moon Paths are meant to be portal like, or wormhole like, but connecting umbral locations, rather than location in the physical world - as moon bridges do. This would fit the 2nd Edition corebook that sates on page 176:<br /> <i>A Garou simply decides where she wants to go - a Near Realm, for example steps onto a Moon Path, and begins walking. The time it takes to travel to certain locations varies - seemingly without rhyme or reason, although some Theurges say this fluctuation involves moon phase, season and environment.</i><br /> <br /> However, there are spirit gates that are the equivalent of portals from one place to another. But, this depiction would make moon paths a bit more similar to Dreaming Trods or Shadowland Nihils, I guess.<br /> <br /> But I remember at least one description of moon paths being just paths of reflected moon light, running trough the umbra, some times elevating into the sky... But I can't seem to find that source and I never bothered to put references into our LARP rules when they were written some 15 to 20 years ago.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1444098-moon-paths-moon-glows-and-penumbral-hazards?p=1444223#post1444223\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Moon Paths being permanent and leading to fixed destinations is probably the easiest interpretation for the ST. They just need to decide where to plant any Moon Paths on his umbral map and determine where they go. I think the only hard decision is deciding how many Moon Paths should be out there and their destinations. I like to have maps in my head (or on paper) and know many important landmarks before I run my games, so I am probably making this harder on myself than most STs who likely only put a Moon Path in after they decide they need one.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, you can start with one or two moon paths that pass by in the vicinity of the place the PCs are. Each moon path has two directions PCs could go. Just keep some of them strictly in the penumbra (passing into the black nothingness of the near umbra and back without hitting any real landmarks there). By this, the moon paths can connect the penumbra of sites you actually use in the game and provide different travel speeds. Meaning, the moon path from near the bawn leads into the near umbra after a mile and re-emerges in the penumbra near the small village chapel. In the physical world, that is 30 miles away, and you would pass through a small wood, cross a river and pass through some shallow hills, where the shrine for the sept's fallen heroes is hidden in a grove. All this landmarks you can't reach, if you take the moon path...<br /> Then, for all other fancy destinations, go from there.... you might end up with a very weird map....<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-16T13:48:16-07:00","id":1444256,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1444098-moon-paths-moon-glows-and-penumbral-hazards?p=1444231#post1444231\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I had not considered the idea that one threat would be Gaian spirits that are predatory, but it's a good idea. Are these mainly spirits of animal predators in your game? Or are they some other kind of predatory spirit? I normally don't have Gaian spirits attack Garou, but am open to the concept. How do you run that in your LARP?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, there are elemental spirits and plant based spirits as well. The latter however are more present in Domains, Moon Paths lead into, as they aren't necessarily present just somewhere in the Near Umbra.<br /> <br /> But it really depends on what we set out to accomplish with a scene or game element.<br /> <br /> We once ran a plot where the PCs had to chase a pride of Ronin. It was a pre-scouted 40 miles hike. The NPCs used a car to drive to a pre-determined location, and wait as an encounter along the route of the PCs who hat to walk. There were several non-wyrm spirit that needed something from the PCs. Fighting - because the PCs passed through their territory, was one, but just wanting to play or playing tricks on the PCs was also part of the encounters. But, the plot was a unique thing, so far.<br /> <br /> In most cases the PCs travel only within the penumbra and through anchorheads into domains, they want to destroy. Random encounters are rare. Other travel is done in the downtime, mostly, so it is governed by hand-waiving. But Moon Glows usually get the PCs a lot of consideration when it comes to the question, if the downtime plans they have work, or if we need to set up a special event to play through some encounter...<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Regarding the Lunes. We assume that there is one or a group of lunes on patrol along the moon paths. Meaning, not every mile is constantly observed by a lune to act as police, but regularly one will encounter a lune in these paths. As for the moon path that passes by near the caern bawn, a lune will be found along this path within an hour of travel from the caern. The garou stuck a bargain with that lune. The lune will replenish all rage to any member or guest of the sept. As payment, the garou must some physical challenge, in form of a contest, usually, for each gathering that is not a formal moot (and therefore doesn't have a Revel).<br /> So, if a player decides his character needs Rage really badly, she can leave the game for an hour, perform some antagonist NPC duties, and then return with her character all rage replenished. Also, Players must come up with some sort of worthy activity for all players, if they decide to not perform a formal moot, leaving them occupied, while the STs can work on their evil schemes...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-16T16:18:11-07:00","id":1444269,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1444098-moon-paths-moon-glows-and-penumbral-hazards?p=1444250#post1444250\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This would fit the 2nd Edition corebook that sates on page 176:</div> </div> </div> </div>Usually when I investigate things I look up rules from different editions, but didn't in this case. Now that I do, it seems 2nd edition says Moon Paths are used to travel to the Near Realms and other places deeper in the Umbra (it's implied this does not work for the Penumbra), and that the Garou can determine his destination for himself. This was probably a place holder explanation of how to reach the Near Realms.<br /> <br /> Revised certainly contradicts that - some Near Realms are definitely harder to visit than others, and we're given examples of what does and doesn't work. However, I think the 2nd edition corebook was really the first corebook to codify some of these things like travelling further into the Umbra. I know the 1st edition corebook doesn't mention Moon Paths at all. I have never seen the original Umbra: the Velvet Shadow of first edition, so I don't know what they say about it. So rather than say Revised contradicts it, it's probably best to say it superceded the original rules. The writers were figuring things out and made adjustments along the way.<br /> <br /> I don't think the second edition version of &quot;find a Moon Path and go where you want&quot; works best for the game. It's just too easy and undermines some of the spiritual struggle/journey aspect of the game. But I do like the idea that a &quot;single&quot; Moon Path could lead to multiple destinations instead of just one. I also think it fits the Revised rules set better now that I think about. (It increases the chances of arriving at the wrong destination if the Moon Path is used during another moon phase.) A Moon Path might not lead to everywhere, but like a train route there could be various places one can get off, including a station to board another train route.<br /> <br /> It makes sense that all Moon Paths could be used to reach the Aetherial Realm. And there might be one or more additional Near Realms it might reach. And possibly one or more destinations in the Penumbra. The Moon Path may only have one possible destination (plus the Aetherial Realm), a few, or many. The ST just needs to decide what is possible for that one specific Path.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-16T16:23:09-07:00","id":1444271,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1444098-moon-paths-moon-glows-and-penumbral-hazards?p=1444250#post1444250\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">However, there are spirit gates that are the equivalent of portals from one place to another. But, this depiction would make moon paths a bit more similar to Dreaming Trods or Shadowland Nihils, I guess.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1444098-moon-paths-moon-glows-and-penumbral-hazards?p=1444250#post1444250\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just keep some of them strictly in the penumbra (passing into the black nothingness of the near umbra and back without hitting any real landmarks there). By this, the moon paths can connect the penumbra of sites you actually use in the game and provide different travel speeds.</div> </div> </div> </div>Before this I had not given much thought to the &quot;inbetween&quot; portion of the Penumbra to Domains, Near Realms, and anything else. Combined with your comparison to Nihils in the Shadowlands, I am not wondering if the process of going &quot;deeper&quot; into the Umbra is much like entering the Tempest in Wraith in that it is a misty, cloudy vista that acts as an intermediary space between the destinations you want to reach. Just without it being a storm or being anywhere near as hazardous it is for wraiths.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-17T10:52:40-07:00","id":1444358,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1444098-moon-paths-moon-glows-and-penumbral-hazards?p=1444271#post1444271\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Before this I had not given much thought to the &quot;inbetween&quot; portion of the Penumbra to Domains, Near Realms, and anything else. Combined with your comparison to Nihils in the Shadowlands, I am not wondering if the process of going &quot;deeper&quot; into the Umbra is much like entering the Tempest in Wraith in that it is a misty, cloudy vista that acts as an intermediary space between the destinations you want to reach. Just without it being a storm or being anywhere near as hazardous it is for wraiths.</div> </div> </div> </div>So I am actually working on a somewhat similar project to you, trying to get a better understanding of the mechanics and nature of the Umbra in order to figure out the background for my setting <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> From what I've read so far, using a mix of Werewolf and Mage sources, you are indeed correct that moving out of the Penumbra and into the Near Realms (in the Middle Umbra at least) is often a matter of going away from the more 'defined' parts connected with the Material and into the &quot;Mists,&quot; though there are also elements of symbolism and omens, where you'll start moving into places that no longer correlate with the Material but instead represent part of your journey in a spiritual or metaphorical way.<br /> <br /> I think the actual process, put somewhat reductively, is:<br /> <br /> 1) Find somewhere in the Penumbra that is associated with the Near Realm you want to reach.<br /> <br /> 2) Go into the &quot;Mists&quot; or some Nowhere-Place (e.g. a Cave that doesn't correspond to anything in the Material Realm), perhaps following some spiritual omen indicating the path<br /> <br /> 3) Travel through the metaphorical steps of your journey, in mist or shadow, until you find the entrance or Pericarp of the Realm you were seeking (assuming you succeed, the Umbra is a messy place).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-17T13:26:18-07:00","id":1444380,"title":"","content":"That mirrors my own thinking, but you made certain things explicit. It departs from what's written in the corebook only in the sense that one navigates first to a location of correspondence and then goes deeper, rather than simply go deeper first and then wander to their destination (which could still happen, it's just a lot more ineffiecient and inept). But it better fits how Umbra: the Velvet Shadow describes things.<br /> <br /> It's also a good transition effect from going from the Penumbra to a Domain. <br /> <br /> I'm now wondering if Moon Paths are found only or at least pre-dominantly in this intermediate mist space so it can take Garou on paths directly to Near Realms or somewhere else &quot;deeper.&quot; Moon Paths in the Penumbra only occur if one of their destinations is in the Penumbra, and are probably of the rare kind.<br /> <br /> We're told that a Garou who follows Luna with much devotion may be rewarded with a vision of a Moon Path. I take that to mean a favored Garou who impresses her, who wants to go someplace, learns of the location of a Moon Path to take him there. A Moon Path &quot;hidden&quot; in these indetermediate Umbral mists works better, than one in the Penumbra whose presence should be well known.<br /> <br /> This leads to some interesting conclusions.<br /> <br /> 1) While a Moon Glow talen may be useful in the Penumbra, it's real purpose is to protect Garou on one of these extended Umbral voyages.<br /> <br /> 2) In terms of &quot;dire spirits&quot; that threaten the Moon Paths; these spirits - whether they be Banes or other hostile spirits - are more likely some kind of spirit &quot;native&quot; to this interdimensional realm rather than the typical spirits found in the Penumbra. Such Penumbral spirits do travel through these intermediate mists (either for shortcuts between the Penumbra, Domains, or to one of the Near Realms) because they produce spirit airts. But it might be best to create brand new spirits that occupy these mists. It would help distinguish this &quot;layer&quot; of the Umbra, and define the typical menaces that a Moon Glow protects.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-17T13:41:00-07:00","id":1444384,"title":"","content":"I must admit, I haven't really looked at the Talen, and I wasn't reading too closely when I read about Moon Paths; going back to read the section in W20's Umbra - tVS, it emphasizes that where they appear and where they lead can be unpredictable. I imagine knowledge of Moon Paths is mostly a local, or perhaps regional, thing that has to update over time as the Moon Paths appear, disappear, and change. I would read that as indicating that a Moon Path is as likely to lead to another part of the Penumbra as it is deeper into the Umbra. It just depends on the particular Moon Path.<br /> <br /> It does seem from my reading that it is actually more &quot;typical&quot; spirits that you might find in the Penumbra rather than entities distinctive to the Moon Paths. Sometimes it has to do with forces of the Triat vying for control over the Path, sometimes its the Lunes themselves. Even regarding the other spirits you might encounter, I'd be inclined to see things with a lunar theme being more likely than something focused on the &quot;mist.&quot; But that's just my interpretation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","user":"Kharnov","date":". 04-17-2021, 04:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-17T16:28:19-07:00","id":1444401,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1444098-moon-paths-moon-glows-and-penumbral-hazards?p=1444384#post1444384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It does seem from my reading that it is actually more &quot;typical&quot; spirits that you might find in the Penumbra rather than entities distinctive to the Moon Paths. Sometimes it has to do with forces of the Triat vying for control over the Path, sometimes its the Lunes themselves. Even regarding the other spirits you might encounter, I'd be inclined to see things with a lunar theme being more likely than something focused on the &quot;mist.&quot; But that's just my interpretation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Certainly Triatic spirits should comprise some of the threats. I'd still like the form of such spirits to make sense rather than pulling the standard Triatic spirits from books simply because that's what we have. But certain of those spirits would be more appropriate to others.<br /> <br /> The most appropriate kind of spirits to bedevil Moon Paths would likely be some kind of corrupted Night spirit or Abyssal spirits given that when Lunes are out (aka moonlight) these spirits stay away, but as the moonlight weakens those spirits become more of a menace until at the time of the new moon, those spirits are completely triumphant in the dark.<br /> <br /> The easiest thing would be to invert the Lunes stats so that these Night/Abyssal spirits have the lowest Rage on nights of the full moon and their highest rage during the new moon. Perhaps make their stats a little bit lower than Lunes so it's not a completely equal, but inverse comparison. We may want an individual Lune to be more powerful than an individual counterpart spirit. Other similar menacing evil night spirits could also be used - like corrupted Bat spirits!<br /> <br /> I think something like that would be more appropriate than, say, grabbing random Banes like a Hoggling, an Ooralath, and a Scrag. Those don't fit the theme of strange spirits that menace travelers on moonless nights, or would flee from a Moon Glow because they think its a Lune. A nocturnal style spirit would be more likely to do that than a Furmling.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-17T16:47:52-07:00","id":1444406,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1444098-moon-paths-moon-glows-and-penumbral-hazards?p=1444401#post1444401\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The easiest thing would be to invert the Lunes stats so that these Night/Abyssal spirits have the lowest Rage on nights of the full moon and their highest rage during the new moon. Perhaps make their stats a little bit lower than Lunes so it's not a completely equal, but inverse comparison. We may want an individual Lune to be more powerful than an individual counterpart spirit. Other similar menacing evil night spirits could also be used - like corrupted Bat spirits!</div> </div> </div> </div>So I like all of this post, but especially the idea about inverting the Lunes' cycle, and also the nod to our other conversation lol","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-17T19:01:45-07:00","id":1444423,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1444098-moon-paths-moon-glows-and-penumbral-hazards?p=1444384#post1444384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I must admit, I haven't really looked at the Talen, and I wasn't reading too closely when I read about Moon Paths; going back to read the section in W20's Umbra - tVS, it emphasizes that where they appear and where they lead can be unpredictable. I imagine knowledge of Moon Paths is mostly a local, or perhaps regional, thing that has to update over time as the Moon Paths appear, disappear, and change. I would read that as indicating that a Moon Path is as likely to lead to another part of the Penumbra as it is deeper into the Umbra. It just depends on the particular Moon Path.</div> </div> </div> </div>It seems each of the editions give slightly different details to Moon Paths. That may be because each edition's writer is reinterpreting them.<br /> <br /> I have not played Werewolf as much as many people on this forum, but I can say I don't remember Moon Paths ever being a prominent part of gameplay. I don't remember an ST ever using one. Though it is possible an ST simply handwaved a Moon Path into existence so the PCs could move onto their next destination in the Umbra, and I simply forgot a Moon Path was involved. I'm thinking maybe that is the case for most chronicles. Though certainly not all as we know Heinrich's LARP makes extensive use of them. As such, maybe their lack of use means everyone interprets them on their own and gets slightly different practical facts.<br /> <br /> There's a lot like that in Werewolf and the other WoD games. There's some great flavor text and some specifics of what something does, but when you go to run it in game you suddenly realize there are a lot of gaps in terms of how to apply it.<br /> <br /> I'm not a fan of the idea of where a Moon Path leads is unpredictable (at least outside using one during the Crescent Moon because that's the peril of using it during that time) because I think that makes them much less useful in game. If a Moon Path has been explored and we know it goes to X (or even that it can be used to go to X,Y and Z), then that becomes useful knowledge the PCs may want to exploit. Then if they decide they have to use one right now during the time of a crescent moon, then that is a risk they willingly take in order to get to X immediately. On the other hand, if the destination is always unpredictable, most PCs will simply choose to never use Moon Paths because it doesn't help them achieve their goals and will likely only delay them longer.<br /> <br /> I'm definitely glad the thread has lead to this discussion because having multiple people work things through helps me to decide of how this can be actually used in game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-17T19:33:42-07:00","id":1444430,"title":"","content":"I myself have very little experience playing with the systems in general, and Werewolf is not really the top of my list either, haha. For the most part, I'm looking at things through the 20A lines, but moving back into older materials for clarification or when they're the only things available.<br /> <br /> From what I've gathered, Moon Paths are like spontaneous Moon Bridges that don't necessarily connect to Caerns. They still seem to run through the sky, though not necessarily reaching as high as the Bridges between Caerns. Apologies for giving the wrong impression, but by &quot;unpredictable&quot; I don't mean &quot;every trip on the Moon Path will lead to a different destination,&quot; but rather &quot;they move over time, sometimes switching faster, sometimes switching slower.&quot; Some Moon Paths might remain stable for years, others months, another days. I was recently pondering the idea of Moon Paths that appear under very specific conditions, like &quot;our Sept has noticed that this Moon Path appears on the full moon of April every 23 lunar years.&quot; The text talked about factions fighting over Moon Paths for their strategic value, so they can't be completely random.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-17T20:37:44-07:00","id":1444435,"title":"","content":"Yes, there are lots of similarities between Moon Paths and Moon Bridges. It's mostly a matter of how they are created. Paths seem to be natural phenomenon - &quot;gifts of Luna&quot; - while Bridges are artificial creations at caerns by the Garou.<br /> <br /> I do think it's perfectly fine for a mix of Moon Paths. Some appear solely to help a spirit quest of a Garou especially devoted to Luna and then disappear. Others are permanent or at least long term and stable. Others seem stable, but only appear at some kind of frequency or interval like you suggested. I think a mix is fine, but for gaming purposes there needs to be some kind of stability for them to be useful to the Garou. The others just become flavor text, or perhaps an excuse for a random adventure.<br /> <br /> I think a harder question is to determine how many (stable/useful) Moon Paths might be &quot;typical&quot; within the range of a sept's protectorate. The books given us no direction at all. That both empowers the individual ST, but can also make it overwhelming to decide how many is a good number for their chronicle. There's a lot of things that require the ST to decide on. And I, at least, can sometimes shut down and entirely ignore something if I feel like I don't have any guidance at all.<br /> <br /> You may just want to start with just one in your setting, and as you get comfortable add more as needed, and then stop once you feel there is enough.<br /> <br /> But I tend to have a lot of pain-in-the-ass players who want to know a lot of things up front for RP purposes. And if I decide to introduce a new Moon Path (that was always supposed to be there), sometimes I get responses of PCs feeling angry at the NPCs for &quot;not telling them that before.&quot; Of course they couldn't because it didn't exist until I just decided. Of course I could just tell this is completely new, but that tends to hurt the idea that there's a history to the setting. And I can tell them that this is new because I just created it as a retcon element, but that always takes us out of the game.<br /> <br /> So my preference is to figure out what is a good amount to include up front that may or may not come into play. So that comes into things like is 4 a good number? 6? What about 9?<br /> <br /> Maybe 3 should be the magic number. Use one that connects points in the Penumbra. Have another that connects to one or more Near Realms that are the typical destinations for Garou like the Legendary Realm or Scar. And one that connects to a useful Domain - whether it be a good ally to the caern, or a frequent enemy. Maybe one of them has something special about them like the examples you gave of only appearing at a certain time or condition. And anything else make up on the fly or known to be random or recent as background flavor. Not too many, but enough to cement the concept in the minds of the players, and allows the ST to play around with the details. And they don't need to be readily available. Some of them might be hard to get to from the caern. It's fine for the ST to want less or more, but as a ground rule maybe 3 is a good way to go.<br /> <br /> = = =<br /> <br /> In terms of other spirit menaces, I've given some thought of other things to steal. The first edition Werewolf Storyteller's Handbook had a bane called Unakas I think could be used to haunt Moon Paths. They appear like undead skeletons and seek to devour spiritual energy. Sounds like something that would set up ambushes at Paths. And I think there are a lot of flavor text that can be stolen from other authors. William Hope Hodgson wrote some cool horror stories of creatures that might be useful - Pneumavores of the Nightland, the various Outer Monstrosities of Carnacki the Ghost Finder, Swine Things in the House at the Borderlands. You might just use the statistics for Scrags, but by stealing descriptions they can seem more interesting and appropriate. Lovecraft is another good source to steal from - Nightgaunts are very cool looking, and the astral terrors in From Beyond also fit. As well as other creatures in the Call of Cthulhu RPG - I think Desh and Dimensional Shamblers could be reskinned. I even think some monsters from D&amp;D could be useful like the Devourers or the various kinds of Nightshades (Nightcrawler, Nightwing, Nightwalker).<br /> <br /> Maybe there are Scryers serving minor Bane lords that keep watch on known Moon Paths, and they minute they see Garou enter them, they report back and whatever servants of that Bane jaggling lord show up like sharks following chum thrown in the ocean.<br /> <br /> Some of these could easily be used elsewhere. Maybe on the nights of the new moon or during eclipses they escape the intermediate mists and can enter the Penumbra. Or certain ones can be summoned by Wyrm cultists. Or they are just present in the skies of the Penumbral night in limited numbers to begin with.<br /> <br /> This would give the ST some tools to decide if they want to use some of these spirits randomly if the PCs travel the Penumbra on nights when the full moon is not out, in order to create conditions where a Moon Glow might become more useful.<br /> <br /> During the daytime, it's know that Weaver spirits are very numerous and active, so PCs should be avoiding the Penumbra during the day unless they use a Moon Glow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-17T22:15:46-07:00","id":1444445,"title":"","content":"I think the best answer to &quot;how many stable Moon Paths should an area have&quot; is probably &quot;as many as you need for the story you want to tell, then maybe a dash more so you can pretend things are a bit more &quot;organic&quot; or &quot;random.&quot;&quot; As you noted, they are essentially a gift from Luna, so their presence is contingent on &quot;divine&quot; (Storyteller) mandate. But Luna is also known for being rather mercurial.<br /> <br /> I do agree that World of Darkness books have a bad habit of leaving you a bit unsure about how to apply particular mechanics or fluff at times. Maybe you get a better idea of what the intent is if you read the fiction series, but they could do a better job of conveying it in the core texts sometimes. Speaking of, I'm trying to figure out if Moon Paths convey the same advantage as Moon Bridges, compressing distance (or time) so that longer journeys can be completed in a relatively short period.<br /> <br /> You've definitely got some great ideas for potential spirits to menace travelers on the Moon Paths! I'm not especially familiar with the vast assortment of spirits that have been written up over the years, I will need to spend some time going through what is already out there. I also need to learn a bit more about the Umbral Winds that you were discussing earlier, and other more generic Umbral hazards. I've been trying to learn more about the Umbra in part because I'm curious about the risks of Umbral travel for Garou over medium-to-long distances, in general but especially in urban environments. I hadn't actually heard about Weaver-spirits being more active in the day before.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","user":"Kharnov","date":". 04-18-2021, 01:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-17T22:38:13-07:00","id":1444447,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1444098-moon-paths-moon-glows-and-penumbral-hazards?p=1444445#post1444445\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Speaking of, I'm trying to figure out if Moon Paths convey the same advantage as Moon Bridges, compressing distance (or time) so that longer journeys can be completed in a relatively short period.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would say yes, or what would be their point? Moon Bridges seem to be a special type of Moon Path so they should function similarly.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1444098-moon-paths-moon-glows-and-penumbral-hazards?p=1444445#post1444445\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also need to learn a bit more about the Umbral Winds that you were discussing earlier, and other more generic Umbral hazards. I've been trying to learn more about the Umbra in part because I'm curious about the risks of Umbral travel for Garou over medium-to-long distances, in general but especially in urban environments. I hadn't actually heard about Weaver-spirits being more active in the day before.</div> </div> </div> </div>Umbra: the Velvet Shadow Revised lists some common umbral hazards on pages 27-28.<br /> <br /> Previous editions of the game had a section called Night in the Umbra chapter which discussed what time is safest for Garou entering the Umbra. It implies the daytime is dangerous because Weaver spirits are very active. I can't find a similar section in the W20 core though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-17T22:57:08-07:00","id":1444452,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1444098-moon-paths-moon-glows-and-penumbral-hazards?p=1444447#post1444447\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I would say yes, or what would be their point? Moon Bridges seem to be a special type of Moon Path so they should function similarly.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Umbra: the Velvet Shadow Revised lists some common umbral hazards on pages 27-28.<br /> <br /> Previous editions of the game had a section called Night in the Umbra chapter which discussed what time is safest for Garou entering the Umbra. It implies the daytime is dangerous because Weaver spirits are very active. I can't find a similar section in the W20 core though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Even without time/distance compression, I can conceive of a few potential advantages for Moon Paths. The first being the protection of the Lunes, at least some of the time. The second being, if it is actually a kind of sky-bridge over the Penumbra, it might allow you to avoid known obstacles or threats below that might otherwise impede your travel. And finally, in the case of the more stable Moon Paths, the simple guarantee that following the Path will reliably lead from Point A to Point B, without all the various risks of getting lost or turned around or stumbling into an unexpected Zone or Domain that might occur if you just set out into the Penumbra in the direction of your destination.<br /> <br /> To the extent that a Moon Bridge is explicitly constructed and powered by Caerns, you can imagine it possessing superior qualities to the more natural and spontaneous Moon Path. Hence my hope for a textual clarification.<br /> <br /> Thanks for the tip on somewhere to find examples of Umbral hazards! I might look into previous editions of Werewolf for more info on Weaver-spirits and the daytime, and also the dangers of Weaver-spirits to Garou traveling through the Penumbra.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-27T09:21:47-07:00","id":1446109,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1444098-moon-paths-moon-glows-and-penumbral-hazards?p=1444452#post1444452\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Even without time/distance compression, I can conceive of a few potential advantages for Moon Paths. The first being the protection of the Lunes, at least some of the time. The second being, if it is actually a kind of sky-bridge over the Penumbra, it might allow you to avoid known obstacles or threats below that might otherwise impede your travel. And finally, in the case of the more stable Moon Paths, the simple guarantee that following the Path will reliably lead from Point A to Point B, without all the various risks of getting lost or turned around or stumbling into an unexpected Zone or Domain that might occur if you just set out into the Penumbra in the direction of your destination.<br /> <br /> To the extent that a Moon Bridge is explicitly constructed and powered by Caerns, you can imagine it possessing superior qualities to the more natural and spontaneous Moon Path. Hence my hope for a textual clarification.<br /> <br /> Thanks for the tip on somewhere to find examples of Umbral hazards! I might look into previous editions of Werewolf for more info on Weaver-spirits and the daytime, and also the dangers of Weaver-spirits to Garou traveling through the Penumbra.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> First, I want to thak all the participants for this very insightful thread. Second, my PCs are escorting some Mages deep into the Umbra and the Moon Glow Talen looks like it will be very useful!<br /> <br /> Finally, here is how I handle Moon Paths.<br /> <br /> * They are mostly stable paths that offer varying levels of protection depending on the time of the month, and they are pretty darn reliable.<br /> * For the most part they run along the umbral ground unless the destination requires one to go skyward.<br /> * They do not shorten travel distance as a Moon Bridge does, but travel time can be cut due to their benefit of being a &quot;safe, reliable route&quot;.<br /> <br /> I love the idea of traveling from the Penumbra into the Near Umbra, and then taking a Moon Path back into the Penumbra farther away as a time cutting measure. This will come in really handy when a nearby Caern is not available (or friendly).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/693-thomasm","name":"ThomasM","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar693_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-29T17:21:02-07:00","id":1446528,"title":"","content":"Now that I have a better understanding of likely hazards in the Umbra that a Moon Glow can avoid, I think this will become a more important Talen. And one that PCs may want to create themselves. So the next question is what kind of chiminage would be appropriate to convince a Lune to be bound to this Talen.<br /> <br /> Talens require less chiminage than Fetishes, but the spirit is still performing one defined service to the Talen's user/creator. And typically, one performs an equivalent like minded service to a spirit in exchange for what it does for you. It's not restricted to this, but a general guideline to evaluate chiminage. We also know that Lunes are well disposed to Garou, so they are likely to be friendly and receptive to helping them, reducing the price. They're also very mercurial and chaotic, and their mood swings with the moon's cycles.<br /> <br /> So what does the Talen actually do? It protects the Garou, but not by fighting for them. It's more like hiding them from their enemies, scaring them off, or otherwise deceiving them for a specified trip. So what should a Lune want in exchange?<br /> <br /> Axis Mundi doesn't include Lunes per se, but it does include a variety of moon spirits and their descriptions include a general chiminage section showing what each one likes. They provide the following examples of chiminage:<ul><li>bloody sacrifices of Luna's and Gaia's enemies</li> <li>helping the harvest moon prepare people for the upcoming winter</li> <li>set right offenses done against Luna/Gaia</li> <li>allowing the spirit to possess the Garou for a period of time</li> </ul>They're all very different given that each was for a different aspect of Luna's brood. But we can see they are somewhat generic in the sense they're not very tied to the moon, and could work with other kinds of spirits. We might also decide that this means what a Lune asks for may be very different depending on the cycle of the moon when it is done. A Lune during the full moon might demand something very warlike or bloody, while during a crescent or new moon might be more spiritually symbolic, meditative, or random.<br /> <br /> Any ideas would be welcomed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-29T23:04:26-07:00","id":1446563,"title":"","content":"In our LARP talen creation is rarely done at the scene, but mostly done in the computer-aided character management tool. We do not require specific chiminage, but an appropriate raw material to inhabit. The garou are required to put time and effort into collecting of crafting this raw talen, which is the show of their dedication. With Moon Glows it is the harvesting of appropriate crystal pieces. It would be possible to trade for the raw pieces, or be gifted them as price for a competition or a well done job, though. Basically, every interaction that does underline or add to the worth of the raw talens, rather than diminishing it.<br /> <br /> And, of course the Rite must be performed satisfactory. We estimate the successes a ritemaster might have and see this as the appropriate number of raw talens he should present during the Rite. If he chooses to present more, we raise the difficulty. We also raise it, when the spirit is more powerful, but grant free successes if at least one regular one was scored.<br /> <br /> Besides that, we work under the assumption that tales don't loose power, until activated. But the spirit ceases to exist, while his essence is spread in possibly multiple talens. Only to reform if a sufficient amount of talens is used. In this regard the differ from fetishes which inhabit the complete spirit and the spirit can be communicated with through meditation.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Oh, we also assume that the number of successful, failed and botched attempts at the Rite of Binding factor into the difficulty. As well as the time elapsed since. So, trying and failing, trying and failing is something that offends or annoys the spirits, raising the difficulty further.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1008,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","user":"heinrich","date":". 04-30-2021, 02:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-30T09:26:07-07:00","id":1446616,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1444098-moon-paths-moon-glows-and-penumbral-hazards?p=1446528#post1446528\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now that I have a better understanding of likely hazards in the Umbra that a Moon Glow can avoid, I think this will become a more important Talen. And one that PCs may want to create themselves. So the next question is what kind of chiminage would be appropriate to convince a Lune to be bound to this Talen.<br /> <br /> Talens require less chiminage than Fetishes, but the spirit is still performing one defined service to the Talen's user/creator. And typically, one performs an equivalent like minded service to a spirit in exchange for what it does for you. It's not restricted to this, but a general guideline to evaluate chiminage. We also know that Lunes are well disposed to Garou, so they are likely to be friendly and receptive to helping them, reducing the price. They're also very mercurial and chaotic, and their mood swings with the moon's cycles.<br /> <br /> So what does the Talen actually do? It protects the Garou, but not by fighting for them. It's more like hiding them from their enemies, scaring them off, or otherwise deceiving them for a specified trip. So what should a Lune want in exchange?<br /> <br /> Axis Mundi doesn't include Lunes per se, but it does include a variety of moon spirits and their descriptions include a general chiminage section showing what each one likes. They provide the following examples of chiminage:<ul><li>bloody sacrifices of Luna's and Gaia's enemies</li> <li>helping the harvest moon prepare people for the upcoming winter</li> <li>set right offenses done against Luna/Gaia</li> <li>allowing the spirit to possess the Garou for a period of time</li> </ul>They're all very different given that each was for a different aspect of Luna's brood. But we can see they are somewhat generic in the sense they're not very tied to the moon, and could work with other kinds of spirits. We might also decide that this means what a Lune asks for may be very different depending on the cycle of the moon when it is done. A Lune during the full moon might demand something very warlike or bloody, while during a crescent or new moon might be more spiritually symbolic, meditative, or random.<br /> <br /> Any ideas would be welcomed.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like the idea that the nature of the chiminage required would shift with the phase of the Moon, seems pretty consistent with Lune behaviour. And I agree that it is likely that the amount of chiminage required for convince a Lune to assist a Garou would be relatively low, one in good standing with Gaia anyways.<br /> <br /> Here are a few ideas for relatively light chiminage:<ul><li>Howling at the appropriate phase of the moon at midnight</li> <li>Organizing a brawl or &quot;fight club&quot; under the light of the full moon</li> <li>Organizing a wild overnight party</li> <li>Spend the night playing riddle-games with the Lune</li> <li>Just getting a bunch of New Age types together at night to do a prayer-circle praising &quot;the moon goddess&quot; while burning incense</li> </ul>Basically, anything that you could imagine generating a little bit of Essence for Luna and her moon-spirits, through action, emotion, veneration, etc. If we're talking a Garou in good standing with Gaia and Luna, it seems reasonable that the Lune would be willing to &quot;help out&quot; without a huge price-tag attached. The Lune isn't being expected to do anything dire or dangerous AFAIK, so it doesn't seem likely that the Garou would be expected to take pay a heavy toll either, unless there is a specific reason.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","user":"Kharnov","date":". 04-30-2021, 12:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-30T15:35:23-07:00","id":1446670,"title":"","content":"Those are some good ideas that cover all the moon phases. I think after the ST uses several of those, the PCs will have another examples they could provide their own ideas and use those if they still want to create Moon Glows.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}